WEBVTT

1
00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:53.640
<i>Egypt.</i>

2
00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:57.280
<i>A land of mystery,
intrigue and rich history.</i>

3
00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:01.680
<i>Today, I, the world-renowned
archeologist</i>

4
00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:04.720
<i>Lord Sylvester Carnaby,
present to you...</i>

5
00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:07.280
<i>Hold on.</i>

6
00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.416
- Mommy, I'm...
<i>- Sylvester!</i>

7
00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:09.656
- I can't talk.
<i>- Where have you been?</i>

8
00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:10.960
<i>I haven't heard a peep from you.</i>

9
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.640
Listen, I can't talk right now.
I have a date with...

10
00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:14.920
<i>A date? Oh, my god.</i>

11
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.376
- No, a date with history!
<i>- At last!</i>

12
00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.400
<i>I bet she's pretty.</i>

13
00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:18.800
- Oh, dear.
<i>- And wealthy, too...</i>

14
00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:19.936
- Oh, I'm losing you...
- <i>She must...</i>

15
00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:21.416
- Oh, terrible signal...
<i>- Hello. Hello.</i>

16
00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:22.440
Oh, drat!

17
00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.720
<i>On the other side of this door</i>

18
00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:30.120
<i>lies the tomb of Princess Nefer.</i>

19
00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:01.200
No, it can't be.

20
00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:02.280
- Wow!
- Wow!

21
00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:03.920
"Wow?"

22
00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:05.920
It's empty!

23
00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:08.040
The mummy isn't here.

24
00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:09.440
- Let me see!
- No!

25
00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:11.160
- Get back.
- No. I got next!

26
00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:13.680
- You're always like this.
- No, you!

27
00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.000
You and your grasping arms...

28
00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:16.480
- What's this?
- Stop it!

29
00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:17.560
Look. Look at this.

30
00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.240
- Lord Carnaby.
- It seems to speak of...

31
00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.000
- Hello?
- a bridge...

32
00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:25.136
Can someone let me out, please?
I don't like it in here.

33
00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:26.800
From the world of the living...

34
00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:29.360
to the afterlife.

35
00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:30.840
A doorway of sorts to...

36
00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:32.520
a city!

37
00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:35.080
A city where the mummies reside
in the afterlife.

38
00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:36.960
A world of mummies...

39
00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:38.760
under the earth.

40
00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:43.960
- What...
- You two. Get the equipment.

41
00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:52.720
I've found something!

42
00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:11.760
Thank you. I love you too.

43
00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:16.320
With love...

44
00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:18.040
Thut the Charioteer.

45
00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.080
Can I?

46
00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:24.040
Sure.

47
00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:29.280
Why did you stop racing?

48
00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:30.840
You're so young.

49
00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:33.720
Oh, you know, I just want
to give others a chance to win.

50
00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:37.000
Why haven't you found
that special girl

51
00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:38.400
to settle down with, hm?

52
00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:40.800
Well, marriage is forever

53
00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:43.000
and us mummies live forever.

54
00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:44.240
So I think...

55
00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:45.640
not for me.

56
00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:48.280
You rock!

57
00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:51.360
- Hey, Thut!
- We love you, Thut!

58
00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:02.920
What you doing, little brother?

59
00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:07.200
Thut's big return!

60
00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.640
You saw all the fans you still have
at the papyrus shop.

61
00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:19.040
No!

62
00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:20.440
I can't.

63
00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:21.760
Yes, you can.

64
00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:22.840
You're the champ!

65
00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:24.000
I was the champ.

66
00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:25.320
Not anymore.

67
00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:28.360
I can't go back.

68
00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:31.160
Just go home, Sekhem.

69
00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:32.480
I'll get us some food.

70
00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:39.800
There you go, my friend.

71
00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:42.760
- See you next week.
- Yeah, see you next week.

72
00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:51.560
Stop, madam!

73
00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:00.000
Oh, you're very kind.

74
00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:03.320
My basket!

75
00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:04.400
No worries! I got it.

76
00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:15.840
Don't you know to look first
before crossing the street?

77
00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:17.280
Don't you see people crossing?

78
00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:18.680
You had to stop! I was first.

79
00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:20.080
I was the one crossing first!

80
00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:21.360
You had to stop.

81
00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:24.320
Next time, look first!

82
00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.640
They'll give anyone
a driving papyrus these days.

83
00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:39.840
Here we are.
Don't forget your basket.

84
00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:42.520
Oh, thank you very much.

85
00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:10.360
Always.

86
00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:11.440
Always the same.

87
00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:15.000
<i>This city's nice but it's underground</i>

88
00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:18.320
<i>I've lost the music in all this sound</i>

89
00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:21.880
<i>Day after day
With no hint of a change</i>

90
00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.560
<i>The monotony's wearing me down</i>

91
00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:28.640
<i>Thousands of years
Of the same old song</i>

92
00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:32.080
<i>And they expect me to sing along</i>

93
00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:35.560
<i>I'm eager to hear any new melody</i>

94
00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:38.360
<i>Could a good dancing rhythm be wrong</i>

95
00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:42.080
<i>So I will rise beyond this tomb</i>

96
00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:45.240
<i>Where I can shine and be made new</i>

97
00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:49.600
<i>Where I can thrive under the sun</i>

98
00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:52.320
<i>A place to call my home</i>

99
00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:55.920
<i>Open my eyes singing my song</i>

100
00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:59.000
<i>Staying awake but dreaming on</i>

101
00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:03.400
<i>Living a life that is my own</i>

102
00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:06.120
<i>A thousand years from now</i>

103
00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:13.760
Princess, where have you been?

104
00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:15.840
Oh, I...

105
00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:16.920
I needed some...

106
00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:18.360
fresh air.

107
00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:20.400
Oh, Ra, be merciful!

108
00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:22.600
Usi, this place hasn't changed

109
00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:24.160
in thousands of years.

110
00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:25.440
We need change.

111
00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:29.080
What would your father say
if he hears you singing?

112
00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:30.640
You will soon be named

113
00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:32.920
the official successor
of the Pharaoh.

114
00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:36.320
Singing is for entertainers,
not for the rulers of our world.

115
00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:38.160
You can't tell him!

116
00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:43.160
- All right.
- Oh, thank you...

117
00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:45.760
The last thing we need
is to make your father suspicious.

118
00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:48.240
Suspicious of what?

119
00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:49.600
Dad! Of...

120
00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:52.000
- Well...
- Her new suitor.

121
00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:55.240
My new suitor?

122
00:09:55.480 --> 00:09:56.480
Did you forget?

123
00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:02.120
Today, my daughter, the Phoenix Bird

124
00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:04.400
guided by Hathor,
the Goddess of Love...

125
00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:06.720
will choose your future husband.

126
00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:10.120
Today? What do you mean "today"?

127
00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:12.600
That was not in my schedule.
Where is my schedule, please?

128
00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:13.920
Dad! Sorry...

129
00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.400
I mean, Great Pharaoh.

130
00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:17.960
I need at least a hundred more years

131
00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:19.280
before I get engaged!

132
00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:20.360
What if...

133
00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:22.416
What if I don't like him?
What if we don't get along?

134
00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:23.440
What if...

135
00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:26.600
Father, I am not having a bird

136
00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:28.240
decide who I marry.

137
00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:30.280
You know what?

138
00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:32.080
I don't want to get married!

139
00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:38.240
It isn't just any bird!

140
00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:39.640
It's a Phoenix Bird.

141
00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:41.800
Sent by the Goddess of Love herself!

142
00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:44.120
Dad, come on.

143
00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:46.400
The 2000s are the new 1000s.

144
00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:48.120
So, I'm still pretty young.

145
00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:50.360
I have other priorities in my life.

146
00:10:50.720 --> 00:10:51.720
Priorities?

147
00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:54.480
Being a princess, that is your duty!

148
00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:55.880
And that includes marriage.

149
00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:00.680
I know you are nervous,
but you will see.

150
00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:04.040
The Goddess has someone handsome
and exciting in mind for you.

151
00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:16.160
The Goddess Hathor

152
00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:18.400
shall guide the majestic Phoenix

153
00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:20.040
through our kingdom.

154
00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:23.080
Let us open the stargate

155
00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:25.280
for the Phoenix!

156
00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:56.800
Sorry. Wrong recipe.

157
00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:11.680
Now, glorious Phoenix!

158
00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:12.840
Take flight!

159
00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:17.480
We await your destiny.

160
00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:32.000
- Watch out!
- Hey!

161
00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:42.800
The Great Sekhem,
the undefeated boomera...

162
00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:45.040
boomerang...

163
00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:46.840
boomerang guy!

164
00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:49.760
Looks like it found someone.

165
00:12:56.520 --> 00:12:57.720
Oh, false alarm.

166
00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:07.720
Oh, no.

167
00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:11.800
The Phoenix Bird has chosen!

168
00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:12.960
Are you sure?

169
00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:15.600
It swooped down towards a house.

170
00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:33.720
Sorry,
signing was from five to seven.

171
00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:38.520
So, excuse me, where are we going?
Do you...

172
00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:39.600
Do you know who I am?

173
00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:41.200
Hello. Hello?

174
00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:42.960
Am I talking to myself here?

175
00:13:43.280 --> 00:13:45.240
Could you please put me down?

176
00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:46.960
What is it the...

177
00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:48.576
- I don't believe it. Him?
- I don't mean to be rude

178
00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:50.080
but could somebody please tell me...

179
00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:51.960
Pharaoh!

180
00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:54.120
Rise, young man.

181
00:13:54.880 --> 00:13:55.880
I know you.

182
00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:58.800
You are Thut the Charioteer, yes?

183
00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:01.040
Ex-charioteer, Your Majesty.

184
00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:02.600
An ex-charioteer?

185
00:14:02.680 --> 00:14:04.640
I have to marry a guy
whose only talent

186
00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:06.120
is riding around in a circle?

187
00:14:07.480 --> 00:14:08.720
Young Thut.

188
00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:11.000
Today is a joyous day indeed

189
00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:12.880
for the Goddess has chosen you.

190
00:14:15.800 --> 00:14:17.360
Thanks. Cheers. Thank you.

191
00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:18.760
In seven days

192
00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:20.720
you shall wed the Princess Nefer!

193
00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:24.040
Wed?

194
00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:26.120
Hold on. As in marry?

195
00:14:26.200 --> 00:14:27.600
We've never even met.

196
00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:31.000
The crazy driver!

197
00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:32.600
Sorry. This is crazy.

198
00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:33.920
Marry the princess?

199
00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:35.000
This is a lot.

200
00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:36.480
I mean, so many things to consider.

201
00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:37.560
Like, are we compatible?

202
00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:39.560
And that I'm allergic to marriage.

203
00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:40.800
Diagnosed, in fact.

204
00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:43.560
He's right, Dad, he's right!

205
00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:45.640
Sorry, I mean, Great Pharaoh.

206
00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:48.760
If you go against
the Goddess' wishes...

207
00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:51.840
they will cut out your tongue
and pluck out your eyes.

208
00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:53.120
Both eyes?

209
00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:55.600
Kind of brings new meaning
to the expression "Love is blind."

210
00:14:56.880 --> 00:14:59.360
Oh, who doesn't love marriage?

211
00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:01.240
Nefer, I love you...

212
00:15:01.320 --> 00:15:02.720
Where were we honeymooning again?

213
00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:05.960
Could you do the pluck out
of the eyes to me

214
00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:07.520
so that I don't have to see this?

215
00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:11.400
Enough!

216
00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:16.080
It is now your duty
to safeguard this ring

217
00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:17.640
until the day of the wedding.

218
00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:19.560
If anything happens to it...

219
00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:21.336
- they'll cut out...
- Loud and clear.

220
00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:22.680
Eyes and tongue punishment thing.

221
00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:26.080
Destiny has been written.

222
00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:30.920
Let us leave the bride and groom
to get to know each other.

223
00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:45.040
What did you say your name was?

224
00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:46.880
Thut the Charioteer.

225
00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:49.800
Whatever. Let's just get
some things straight, okay?

226
00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:51.736
Don't go getting
emotionally involved because...

227
00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:53.320
Hey, stop, Princess.

228
00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:55.280
Honestly, you're not my type.

229
00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:57.200
Oh, what a relief.

230
00:15:57.280 --> 00:15:58.680
Because I wouldn't go out with you

231
00:15:58.760 --> 00:16:00.560
if you were the last mummy on earth.

232
00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:02.240
So, thanks for saving me the trouble.

233
00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:07.120
Well, you make an eternity
feel like...

234
00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:08.720
an eternity.

235
00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:10.336
Why am I even wasting my time
talking to you?

236
00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:12.240
The woman who needs a deranged
pigeon

237
00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:13.320
to find her a husband.

238
00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:16.920
Oh, it is not a pigeon.

239
00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:19.240
It's a Phoenix Bird!

240
00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:21.720
Sent by the Goddess of Love herself!

241
00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:24.520
Oh, you...

242
00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:26.040
you smile.

243
00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:29.440
Listen, obviously,
there has been some kind of mistake.

244
00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:34.040
Your dad seems like
a reasonable Pharaoh, right?

245
00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:35.760
He can be.

246
00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:37.800
Look, why don't you just back out?

247
00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:39.240
They'd only scoop out your eyes

248
00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:40.936
and cut out your tongue,
and then you'd talk less!

249
00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:42.080
So, win-win.

250
00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:43.680
This is getting dark.

251
00:16:45.160 --> 00:16:46.720
Hey, shouldn't it be

252
00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:48.200
nighttime by now?

253
00:16:48.640 --> 00:16:49.640
Oh, you're right!

254
00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:50.840
Usi!

255
00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:57.680
- Yes?
- Operator, it should be nighttime.

256
00:16:59.320 --> 00:17:00.400
Quickly. Quickly!

257
00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:03.440
Night!

258
00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:46.560
Shooting star, please.

259
00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:53.200
I think I could get used to this.

260
00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:55.640
Well, you won't have to, so...

261
00:17:58.040 --> 00:17:59.200
Thanks for coming by, though.

262
00:17:59.560 --> 00:18:00.640
A shame you have to go.

263
00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:04.080
So, I'll...

264
00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:05.160
see you at the wedding?

265
00:18:05.920 --> 00:18:07.120
I can't wait.

266
00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:09.360
- Well, neither can I.
- Oh, yeah?

267
00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:12.000
Well, I really can't wait
to marry you.

268
00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:13.560
I'm just so excited

269
00:18:13.640 --> 00:18:15.840
- to marry a charioteer!
- Oh, yeah?

270
00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:17.640
Well, I can't wait to marry you

271
00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:19.120
and love you forever

272
00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:20.800
and cherish you for all eternity!

273
00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:21.920
- Fine!
- Fine!

274
00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:27.400
The shooting star was a bit much,
don't you think?

275
00:18:28.680 --> 00:18:30.760
Oh, he seemed nice.

276
00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:31.840
Nice?

277
00:18:32.400 --> 00:18:33.400
Please.

278
00:18:46.280 --> 00:18:48.000
Well? What did they want?

279
00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:50.120
I was afraid
they were going to execute you.

280
00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:52.640
No. It's worse than that.

281
00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:54.640
They want me to get married.

282
00:18:55.040 --> 00:18:56.560
Married? You?

283
00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:03.520
I would lose all my freedom.

284
00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:04.760
I'm pro-single!

285
00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:07.960
How can I be pro-single and married
at the same time?

286
00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:09.040
It's impossible!

287
00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:12.360
Listen, brother.
Let's keep the Thut myth alive.

288
00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:15.160
Nobody can know what I really am.

289
00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:16.680
Not even the princess.

290
00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:19.200
Wait. Did you say "the princess"?

291
00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:21.320
That's awesome!

292
00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:23.600
We're gonna be rich! Like, forever!

293
00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:26.600
And live in the palace!
And have servants that will...

294
00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:28.160
will wipe our rooms for us.

295
00:19:28.240 --> 00:19:30.480
Princess or not,
I don't want to get married.

296
00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:32.720
No matter how many people
might clean for me.

297
00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:34.400
Is that the wedding ring?

298
00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:35.920
It's huge!

299
00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:37.360
- Here, let me have it.
- No.

300
00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:43.920
- It's heavy!
- Yeah, like a ball and chain.

301
00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:46.280
Sekhem, do you take this croc

302
00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:48.600
to be your lawfully wedded crocodile?

303
00:19:48.960 --> 00:19:49.960
Would you give that back?

304
00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:51.440
My life depends on this ring.

305
00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:53.680
I'm not even gonna keep it at home.

306
00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:56.360
This ring is going
where nobody else can get to it.

307
00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:10.120
Your trophies!

308
00:20:11.280 --> 00:20:12.600
Don't touch anything.

309
00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:13.800
Understood?

310
00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:20.080
It will be safe here.

311
00:20:21.960 --> 00:20:22.960
Okay, let's go.

312
00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:45.240
Would you look at that?

313
00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:48.480
It is full of wonderful things!

314
00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:51.480
- Is it my turn now?
- No, I go next.

315
00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:53.256
- No, 'cause it's mine.
- You're always like this.

316
00:20:53.280 --> 00:20:54.440
- I go next!
- Stop it!

317
00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:55.880
This is serious archaeology.

318
00:20:59.080 --> 00:21:00.600
Mother! You'll never guess what...

319
00:21:06.440 --> 00:21:07.440
Careful, you...

320
00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:11.880
You!

321
00:21:17.120 --> 00:21:19.000
What on earth
do you think you're doing?

322
00:21:22.520 --> 00:21:24.480
You only had to hold on to the tablet

323
00:21:24.640 --> 00:21:25.960
and not touch anything.

324
00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:27.680
I gave you one job!

325
00:21:32.800 --> 00:21:34.520
You great big nincom...

326
00:21:34.840 --> 00:21:36.240
Wait. What's that?

327
00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:37.960
Oh, go on then.

328
00:21:41.920 --> 00:21:43.840
A royal wedding ring.

329
00:21:53.480 --> 00:21:54.480
Oh, yes!

330
00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:58.000
What the...

331
00:22:09.440 --> 00:22:10.440
The charioteer?

332
00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:11.760
No. No.

333
00:22:12.320 --> 00:22:13.320
What happened?

334
00:22:16.760 --> 00:22:17.840
The ring, where's the ring?

335
00:22:19.200 --> 00:22:20.200
It's gone!

336
00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:22.360
It's disappeared!

337
00:22:26.760 --> 00:22:29.960
By the god Ra,
this could only be the work of...

338
00:22:31.200 --> 00:22:32.200
Livings!

339
00:22:36.480 --> 00:22:37.880
This will be the jewel

340
00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:39.480
of my new exhibition.

341
00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:43.000
Call the royal guard!

342
00:22:43.080 --> 00:22:45.560
And tell them I lost the ring?
Are you nuts?

343
00:22:45.640 --> 00:22:47.360
It's just a ring. Buy another one.

344
00:22:47.520 --> 00:22:50.080
It's the "Ring." Don't you get it?

345
00:22:50.160 --> 00:22:52.000
If I don't find it,
they'll cut out my tongue

346
00:22:52.080 --> 00:22:53.520
and scoop out my eyes.

347
00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:55.880
The only way to get it back
is to go to...

348
00:22:56.360 --> 00:22:57.360
the world of the living.

349
00:22:57.880 --> 00:23:00.280
Really? Great! What an adventure!

350
00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:02.680
Adventure? It's dangerous!

351
00:23:03.600 --> 00:23:05.400
You're not alone. You have a team.

352
00:23:05.640 --> 00:23:07.200
There is no way you are coming.

353
00:23:07.280 --> 00:23:08.760
They are mummy robbers.

354
00:23:08.840 --> 00:23:11.400
We created this inner city
to be protected from them.

355
00:23:11.720 --> 00:23:12.720
Listen, brother.

356
00:23:12.800 --> 00:23:15.280
Either I come with you,
or I tell the Pharaoh.

357
00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:19.360
May the gods protect us.

358
00:23:59.680 --> 00:24:02.000
Sekhem! We have to avoid
the strong white light.

359
00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:03.880
It would reveal our true nature
to the living.

360
00:24:28.240 --> 00:24:29.240
Look out!

361
00:24:30.920 --> 00:24:31.920
What was that?

362
00:24:32.000 --> 00:24:34.720
A giant chariot.
But where are the horses?

363
00:24:34.920 --> 00:24:35.920
Thut!

364
00:24:43.400 --> 00:24:44.640
There! They've got the ring!

365
00:24:45.680 --> 00:24:47.216
- Nice one, Lord...
- Shut up, would you?

366
00:24:47.240 --> 00:24:48.240
Just do your jobs.

367
00:24:52.440 --> 00:24:54.280
The ring!
This will be easier than I thought.

368
00:24:54.360 --> 00:24:55.360
Wait here.

369
00:25:01.040 --> 00:25:02.680
Right now, get that thing over there

370
00:25:02.760 --> 00:25:03.920
and shove it over there.

371
00:25:06.080 --> 00:25:07.480
Right, there's no space over there.

372
00:25:13.080 --> 00:25:14.520
Sekhem! What are you doing here?

373
00:25:14.720 --> 00:25:16.520
Look! The ring is in
that other steel beast!

374
00:25:16.600 --> 00:25:17.960
What do you mean? Which other one?

375
00:25:18.760 --> 00:25:20.200
Quickly! The beasts are migrating!

376
00:25:26.160 --> 00:25:27.160
Thut, come on!

377
00:25:28.040 --> 00:25:29.680
Thut! Pull yourself up!

378
00:25:32.560 --> 00:25:33.600
What's happened to you?

379
00:25:34.120 --> 00:25:35.280
This is going too fast.

380
00:25:35.360 --> 00:25:37.240
No. Focus on your mission.

381
00:25:38.600 --> 00:25:40.280
That's it, thinking about the ring.

382
00:25:41.200 --> 00:25:42.200
Should be nice and easy.

383
00:25:42.480 --> 00:25:45.120
Open the crate, take the ring,
I keep my eyes.

384
00:25:46.920 --> 00:25:48.240
This could take a while.

385
00:25:54.000 --> 00:25:55.640
Nothing.
It must be in one of the other...

386
00:25:57.120 --> 00:25:58.120
Time to unload!

387
00:25:58.400 --> 00:26:00.120
Someone's coming! Quick, hide!

388
00:26:25.000 --> 00:26:26.000
Go!

389
00:26:26.160 --> 00:26:27.160
Where are we?

390
00:26:27.240 --> 00:26:29.016
Don't worry.
Everything is gonna be all right.

391
00:26:29.040 --> 00:26:31.040
The sooner we find the ring,
the sooner we're home.

392
00:26:31.080 --> 00:26:32.320
Quickly! No time to lose.

393
00:26:34.680 --> 00:26:35.680
We're not alone.

394
00:26:49.480 --> 00:26:51.040
Oh, what? You?

395
00:26:56.720 --> 00:26:57.720
- Princess!
- Help.

396
00:27:05.640 --> 00:27:06.680
Oh. Princess Nefer's here.

397
00:27:07.200 --> 00:27:09.080
Wait a minute, Princess Nefer?
Why are you here?

398
00:27:09.360 --> 00:27:11.680
The question is why are you here?

399
00:27:12.000 --> 00:27:13.000
Running away?

400
00:27:13.080 --> 00:27:14.080
Running away?

401
00:27:14.480 --> 00:27:16.960
Are you kidding?
Thut runs from nobody!

402
00:27:17.240 --> 00:27:18.320
He's the bravest.

403
00:27:18.560 --> 00:27:20.560
Although, he did lose the ring.

404
00:27:20.640 --> 00:27:22.120
- Sekhem!
- Lost the ring?

405
00:27:22.200 --> 00:27:23.600
No, but that's great!

406
00:27:23.960 --> 00:27:25.496
- Then we don't have to get married!
- No!

407
00:27:25.520 --> 00:27:27.720
That's not great!
That's not great at all!

408
00:27:27.920 --> 00:27:30.120
- They're gonna take my eyes!
- But think...

409
00:27:30.480 --> 00:27:33.640
Eyes. Eternal marriage. Eyes.
Eternal marriage.

410
00:27:33.720 --> 00:27:36.440
Come on! They're not that nice.
You still got four other senses.

411
00:27:36.520 --> 00:27:37.720
They take my tongue, too.

412
00:27:38.520 --> 00:27:40.160
Then you still have
three other senses.

413
00:27:40.240 --> 00:27:42.040
Enough. I don't wanna talk about it.

414
00:27:42.160 --> 00:27:43.160
Let's get out of here.

415
00:27:47.320 --> 00:27:48.480
It's locked from the outside.

416
00:27:48.560 --> 00:27:50.040
We are stuck in here.

417
00:27:50.240 --> 00:27:51.800
Oh, yeah? That's what you think.

418
00:27:52.120 --> 00:27:53.120
Watch and learn.

419
00:27:58.600 --> 00:28:00.800
And I pass into the afterlife!

420
00:28:00.880 --> 00:28:03.320
- I win!
- Congrats, you beat a kid.

421
00:28:05.440 --> 00:28:06.480
How long have I been out?

422
00:28:06.880 --> 00:28:07.880
All night.

423
00:28:08.840 --> 00:28:10.120
Should I tell him? Or you?

424
00:28:10.440 --> 00:28:12.680
- You! You're his brother.
- You're the princess.

425
00:28:12.760 --> 00:28:14.240
- So?
- And his fiancée.

426
00:28:14.320 --> 00:28:16.120
Oh, come on, that doesn't count!

427
00:28:16.640 --> 00:28:17.640
I'm not...

428
00:28:18.360 --> 00:28:19.360
Hey!

429
00:28:21.840 --> 00:28:23.760
Oh, sweet Mother of Horus.

430
00:28:24.200 --> 00:28:25.200
That's the sea!

431
00:28:25.280 --> 00:28:26.680
Oh, well done, genius.

432
00:28:26.760 --> 00:28:28.640
Well, excuse me, Princess.

433
00:28:28.720 --> 00:28:29.800
Maybe we wouldn't be here

434
00:28:29.880 --> 00:28:31.736
- if you hadn't hit me with a...
- Oh, come on, would you relax?

435
00:28:31.760 --> 00:28:33.760
If we escape now,
we'll be lost at sea.

436
00:28:33.840 --> 00:28:35.560
We have to wait until we get to land.

437
00:28:46.760 --> 00:28:48.400
Croc. Shut up.

438
00:28:49.040 --> 00:28:50.040
Croc!

439
00:28:50.840 --> 00:28:51.840
Thank you.

440
00:29:00.120 --> 00:29:01.680
A princess who snores?

441
00:29:01.760 --> 00:29:02.920
And I bet she farts.

442
00:29:31.360 --> 00:29:33.000
That's it. Lower. Lower.

443
00:29:39.560 --> 00:29:41.520
Come on! Let's go.
We have to find the ring.

444
00:29:58.440 --> 00:29:59.440
Sekhem!

445
00:30:01.680 --> 00:30:04.320
Oh, my Osiris.

446
00:30:04.800 --> 00:30:06.120
What place is this?

447
00:30:06.480 --> 00:30:09.160
Amun, I've never seen
anything like it.

448
00:30:09.480 --> 00:30:11.920
- Babylon!
- No, this is way bigger.

449
00:30:12.400 --> 00:30:14.600
There's only one power
that could surpass Egypt.

450
00:30:15.320 --> 00:30:16.480
The Roman Empire!

451
00:30:16.560 --> 00:30:19.560
Exactly. Guys, we are in Rome.

452
00:30:24.560 --> 00:30:26.040
Hey, look at that!

453
00:30:26.360 --> 00:30:28.000
It's the man.
The man who took the ring.

454
00:30:28.080 --> 00:30:29.536
- Give it here. Give it!
- No, I go next!

455
00:30:29.560 --> 00:30:30.776
- You shut your cake hole!
- Careful!

456
00:30:30.800 --> 00:30:32.280
I'm not the uncareful one. No!

457
00:30:32.360 --> 00:30:33.840
Mine. Mine! Be quiet!

458
00:30:34.200 --> 00:30:35.760
Just put it down. Now.

459
00:30:37.480 --> 00:30:38.640
You stupid...

460
00:30:41.880 --> 00:30:42.880
Mother!

461
00:30:43.600 --> 00:30:44.600
The theater?

462
00:30:45.040 --> 00:30:46.840
Of course, Mother,
how could I forget?

463
00:30:47.040 --> 00:30:48.560
Why didn't you idiots remind me

464
00:30:48.640 --> 00:30:50.360
I had tickets to the theater today?

465
00:30:50.760 --> 00:30:51.880
I'm on my way, Mommy.

466
00:30:53.320 --> 00:30:54.320
To the theater.

467
00:31:09.200 --> 00:31:10.200
Quick! Hide!

468
00:31:18.840 --> 00:31:19.840
Yeah.

469
00:31:20.480 --> 00:31:21.680
Oh, I love Romans!

470
00:31:25.800 --> 00:31:27.840
<i>- Have you seen it? You'll love it
- Yes, of course.</i>

471
00:31:30.200 --> 00:31:31.200
<i>What?</i>

472
00:31:32.080 --> 00:31:33.560
<i>Look! It's them!</i>

473
00:31:33.640 --> 00:31:34.960
<i>- I can't believe it!
- It's true!</i>

474
00:31:36.400 --> 00:31:37.720
What are those light rays?

475
00:31:37.800 --> 00:31:39.440
They're stealing our souls!

476
00:31:53.840 --> 00:31:54.840
Is everyone okay?

477
00:31:54.920 --> 00:31:55.920
I'm all right!

478
00:31:56.000 --> 00:31:57.000
Me, too.

479
00:32:01.080 --> 00:32:03.200
The gods are protecting us!
We're saved!

480
00:32:03.480 --> 00:32:05.120
Look! They left their weapons!

481
00:32:05.720 --> 00:32:07.600
Come on, nothing can stop us.

482
00:32:12.200 --> 00:32:13.720
Sylvester! You're late.

483
00:32:14.200 --> 00:32:16.520
But I don't mind
because you've always been

484
00:32:16.600 --> 00:32:18.040
- my little one!
- Oh, Mommy, please.

485
00:32:20.160 --> 00:32:21.160
Not in public. No...

486
00:32:21.680 --> 00:32:23.080
Mommy don't, please.

487
00:32:23.320 --> 00:32:24.320
There. That's better.

488
00:32:24.400 --> 00:32:26.640
Quick! Before he walks into
that brightly lit structure!

489
00:32:30.200 --> 00:32:32.000
Hey, what are you doing here?

490
00:32:33.480 --> 00:32:34.720
Step back, Roman!

491
00:32:37.640 --> 00:32:40.240
- These weapons are useless!
- Okay...

492
00:32:40.320 --> 00:32:41.456
Your Instagram stuff is done.

493
00:32:41.480 --> 00:32:43.360
The front door
is for the audience, honey.

494
00:32:43.440 --> 00:32:44.576
- Come on, here we go. Stage door.
- What? Hey!

495
00:32:44.600 --> 00:32:45.760
- Spit spot!
- Excuse me. Hey!

496
00:32:49.360 --> 00:32:50.360
What?

497
00:32:53.080 --> 00:32:55.000
This is a strange Egyptian colony.

498
00:32:55.360 --> 00:32:56.760
Stay with me. I'll protect you.

499
00:32:57.480 --> 00:32:59.080
Hey, dears, hurry up!

500
00:32:59.400 --> 00:33:01.880
No! Wait.
We're looking for Hathor's ring!

501
00:33:01.960 --> 00:33:03.760
I demand that you tell me
where it is!

502
00:33:05.000 --> 00:33:06.560
You're in character. I like it.

503
00:33:06.640 --> 00:33:07.640
Approved.

504
00:33:07.720 --> 00:33:08.920
Now go and wait for your cue!

505
00:33:10.640 --> 00:33:11.640
Oh! Hey.

506
00:33:12.240 --> 00:33:14.320
- That one is such a diva.
- Oh, yes.

507
00:33:16.480 --> 00:33:17.960
Does this colony have a pharaoh?

508
00:33:18.040 --> 00:33:19.440
You're talking to him, honey.

509
00:33:20.000 --> 00:33:21.000
Ready.

510
00:33:22.880 --> 00:33:25.520
Hey, dears! Come on, here we go,
stage door, spit spot...

511
00:33:30.400 --> 00:33:32.600
<i>That I command</i>

512
00:33:34.120 --> 00:33:41.680
- <i>So I'm here for you now</i>
- Oh, it's beautiful!

513
00:33:44.120 --> 00:33:45.280
Dancers, on!

514
00:33:51.120 --> 00:33:52.600
<i>My lovely Aida</i>

515
00:33:52.680 --> 00:33:55.560
<i>I'll be merciful
To your Nubian people</i>

516
00:33:55.760 --> 00:33:58.480
<i>Me, Radamès
The great general of Egypt</i>

517
00:33:58.760 --> 00:34:02.320
<i>- I offer you my heart
- Oh, great Radamès</i>

518
00:34:02.400 --> 00:34:04.720
<i>I'm so grateful for your mercy...</i>

519
00:34:06.120 --> 00:34:07.800
Excuse me,
we're looking for Hathor's ring.

520
00:34:08.120 --> 00:34:09.440
Anyone seen Hathor's ring?

521
00:34:09.520 --> 00:34:13.600
<i>You are the source and subject
Of all my affection</i>

522
00:34:13.760 --> 00:34:15.480
They sing instead of speak. It's...

523
00:34:15.560 --> 00:34:16.880
It's like their language.

524
00:34:16.960 --> 00:34:18.440
This is amazing!

525
00:34:18.520 --> 00:34:23.000
<i>You're the moon to my ocean</i>

526
00:34:23.240 --> 00:34:24.720
<i>Here is my present</i>

527
00:34:24.800 --> 00:34:30.120
<i>It's the Ring of Love</i>

528
00:34:30.280 --> 00:34:34.000
<i>Oh, great Radamès
I'm sorry to interrupt you</i>

529
00:34:34.080 --> 00:34:36.640
<i>But this ring is mine
This ring is mine</i>

530
00:34:36.720 --> 00:34:37.720
Who is she?

531
00:34:37.960 --> 00:34:39.680
<i>Return it to me, please</i>

532
00:34:39.760 --> 00:34:41.920
<i>My eternal gratitude</i>

533
00:34:42.120 --> 00:34:44.440
<i>Pledge my heart and soul to you</i>

534
00:34:44.720 --> 00:34:48.680
<i>Please give me back my ring</i>

535
00:34:48.880 --> 00:34:50.800
<i>Radamès</i>

536
00:34:51.240 --> 00:34:53.240
<i>Radamès</i>

537
00:34:53.440 --> 00:34:55.400
- <i>Radamès</i>
- That's not in the script.

538
00:34:55.880 --> 00:34:57.760
<i>Radamès</i>

539
00:34:58.080 --> 00:34:59.560
<i>You do not belong here</i>

540
00:34:59.880 --> 00:35:02.000
<i>This is not your show.</i>

541
00:35:02.080 --> 00:35:06.600
<i>Who are you? Where do you come
from?</i>

542
00:35:09.080 --> 00:35:10.560
Where did that voice come from?

543
00:35:10.640 --> 00:35:12.440
She's marvelous!

544
00:35:12.520 --> 00:35:14.760
But she's not in the program at all.
What a bungle.

545
00:35:14.920 --> 00:35:16.080
Do you know her, Sylvester?

546
00:35:16.400 --> 00:35:17.400
Oh! Wake up!

547
00:35:17.840 --> 00:35:19.160
What are you doing?

548
00:35:19.400 --> 00:35:21.000
Asleep all the way through!

549
00:35:21.680 --> 00:35:23.480
Of course, she's trying
to steal my song.

550
00:35:25.600 --> 00:35:27.680
<i>You, slave, get back to your place</i>

551
00:35:27.760 --> 00:35:30.000
<i>You, slave, who do you think you are?</i>

552
00:35:30.080 --> 00:35:31.320
<i>Show us some respect</i>

553
00:35:31.400 --> 00:35:34.640
<i>- Leave me alone with my love
- I'm sorry, but it's mine</i>

554
00:35:34.720 --> 00:35:36.720
<i>Give me the ring. Give me the ring</i>

555
00:35:36.800 --> 00:35:39.600
<i>- Oh, Radamès
- This is Aida's song to sing</i>

556
00:35:39.680 --> 00:35:40.920
<i>Why are you trying</i>

557
00:35:41.000 --> 00:35:43.200
- <i>To steal from me?</i>
- That symbol...

558
00:35:43.640 --> 00:35:44.640
Impossible.

559
00:35:44.720 --> 00:35:47.520
<i>I should probably go now</i>

560
00:35:48.600 --> 00:35:50.240
<i>It's really time to leave</i>

561
00:35:50.320 --> 00:35:53.400
<i>But I can't without this ring</i>

562
00:35:53.760 --> 00:35:55.760
<i>This ring is mine</i>

563
00:35:56.000 --> 00:35:58.000
<i>- This ring is mine
- This ring is mine</i>

564
00:35:58.080 --> 00:36:00.400
<i>- This ring is mine
- This ring is mine</i>

565
00:36:00.480 --> 00:36:08.400
<i>- This ring is mine
- The ring is hers</i>

566
00:36:09.800 --> 00:36:17.400
<i>This ring is mine</i>

567
00:36:19.560 --> 00:36:21.000
<i>This ring is mine</i>

568
00:36:34.400 --> 00:36:36.120
Incredible! Bravo!

569
00:36:36.200 --> 00:36:39.600
That is the best staging
I have ever seen!

570
00:36:40.040 --> 00:36:41.960
This isn't staged.

571
00:36:52.400 --> 00:36:54.120
You like her.

572
00:36:54.200 --> 00:36:55.480
I don't like her.

573
00:36:55.560 --> 00:36:59.440
Yes, you do. You like...

574
00:36:59.800 --> 00:37:02.360
Did you see?
They gave me a standing ovation!

575
00:37:02.440 --> 00:37:04.680
Super! You got an ovation.
I got the ring.

576
00:37:04.760 --> 00:37:06.120
Now, back to the After World.

577
00:37:07.280 --> 00:37:09.600
Oh, look! We can use a human chariot.

578
00:37:11.280 --> 00:37:12.880
Go! Come on!

579
00:37:15.360 --> 00:37:16.360
Why isn't it moving?

580
00:37:18.200 --> 00:37:19.760
Look! The chariot's tied up!

581
00:37:20.160 --> 00:37:21.160
Hey, guys!

582
00:37:22.840 --> 00:37:24.400
Hi! I was looking for you.

583
00:37:24.480 --> 00:37:27.120
- I need to talk to her. She's...
- Thanks, but no thanks.

584
00:37:27.200 --> 00:37:28.200
Wait.

585
00:37:28.360 --> 00:37:30.216
- Why do you need to talk to me?
- I heard you sing in there...

586
00:37:30.240 --> 00:37:32.160
Sorry, sir, but where are the horses?

587
00:37:32.320 --> 00:37:33.720
And how many does this have?

588
00:37:34.280 --> 00:37:35.720
I don't really do cars, but...

589
00:37:36.320 --> 00:37:37.536
It's the grave robber! Come on!

590
00:37:37.560 --> 00:37:39.160
We have to run! He wants the ring!

591
00:37:39.360 --> 00:37:40.760
I'm here to help. Get in!

592
00:37:45.560 --> 00:37:46.560
What?

593
00:37:47.400 --> 00:37:48.400
No!

594
00:37:50.040 --> 00:37:51.040
<i>Sylvester!</i>

595
00:37:51.480 --> 00:37:52.480
Yes, Mother?

596
00:37:53.000 --> 00:37:54.960
Who are you?
Where do you hide the horses, huh?

597
00:37:55.040 --> 00:37:57.600
Please, excuse Thut.
He's just very... Well...

598
00:37:58.640 --> 00:38:00.040
- Who are you?
- Name's Ed.

599
00:38:00.120 --> 00:38:01.440
I came for you for a reason.

600
00:38:01.680 --> 00:38:04.240
I heard you sing in there,
and I absolutely loved your voice.

601
00:38:05.080 --> 00:38:07.640
Well, the joke's on you, pal,
because I didn't even sing.

602
00:38:07.840 --> 00:38:09.360
So I don't know
what you were watching.

603
00:38:09.480 --> 00:38:11.120
Not you, mate. Her.

604
00:38:11.520 --> 00:38:12.920
Me? Yeah?

605
00:38:13.320 --> 00:38:15.736
So I've got a song I've wrote
that I think you'd be perfect for.

606
00:38:15.760 --> 00:38:17.080
Would you like to sing it for me?

607
00:38:18.320 --> 00:38:20.080
- I... I...
- Thanks, Ed.

608
00:38:20.160 --> 00:38:22.400
She would love to, but we really have

609
00:38:22.480 --> 00:38:23.800
more pressing matters.

610
00:38:24.040 --> 00:38:25.520
Could you stop? Please?

611
00:38:32.840 --> 00:38:34.760
Hey, hey think about it,
and get me through

612
00:38:34.840 --> 00:38:35.840
Insta or Facebook.

613
00:38:36.360 --> 00:38:37.520
- Where?
- Thanks! Bye!

614
00:38:37.840 --> 00:38:40.000
Now, can we please focus
on returning home?

615
00:38:44.880 --> 00:38:47.760
I'm sorry about him.
Thank you for saving us.

616
00:38:47.840 --> 00:38:49.720
Hey, if you need me,
you'll find me here.

617
00:38:49.800 --> 00:38:51.600
Sure. Will do.

618
00:39:04.920 --> 00:39:06.240
Why don't you give me a choice?

619
00:39:06.520 --> 00:39:08.520
He has seen
something special in me, Thut.

620
00:39:08.600 --> 00:39:10.760
A choice? None of us have a choice.

621
00:39:10.840 --> 00:39:13.360
We belong in the After World.
You are the Princess.

622
00:39:13.720 --> 00:39:15.440
I have been dreaming all my life

623
00:39:15.520 --> 00:39:17.600
about what I want to do,
and that is singing.

624
00:39:17.880 --> 00:39:19.360
I don't know if I want to go back

625
00:39:19.440 --> 00:39:21.160
and spend an eternity bound to a...

626
00:39:22.280 --> 00:39:24.440
To have my dreams dismissed.

627
00:39:26.400 --> 00:39:27.400
Oh, Ra!

628
00:39:27.480 --> 00:39:29.720
I just wish that stupid bird
never chose me.

629
00:39:32.720 --> 00:39:34.440
Technically, he didn't.

630
00:39:34.520 --> 00:39:36.440
- What?
- What do you mean "technically"?

631
00:39:37.200 --> 00:39:39.200
Well, I knocked it down
with my boomerang.

632
00:39:39.520 --> 00:39:41.880
It's not like he saw you
and chose you or anything.

633
00:39:42.440 --> 00:39:43.760
- Sorry...
- Sekhem!

634
00:39:44.520 --> 00:39:47.040
- You...
- Beautiful boy!

635
00:39:47.560 --> 00:39:48.720
Do you know what this means?

636
00:39:48.800 --> 00:39:51.800
- I get to remain single!
- And I don't have to marry you!

637
00:39:51.880 --> 00:39:54.280
This is the best thing
that could have happened to me!

638
00:39:54.360 --> 00:39:55.360
Me, too!

639
00:40:02.040 --> 00:40:03.760
Okay, let's find a boat to go home.

640
00:40:03.840 --> 00:40:04.840
We're running outta time.

641
00:40:06.640 --> 00:40:08.280
It's a magic stargate.

642
00:40:08.520 --> 00:40:09.920
Maybe we can enter there.

643
00:40:10.000 --> 00:40:12.200
And then home.
Sekhem, you're a genius.

644
00:40:12.280 --> 00:40:13.280
I love it.

645
00:40:13.360 --> 00:40:14.640
Oh, by the way. This is for you.

646
00:40:15.440 --> 00:40:17.360
Hey, guys? This isn't the ring.

647
00:40:17.440 --> 00:40:19.296
Isn't the ring?
What do you mean it isn't the ring?

648
00:40:19.320 --> 00:40:20.720
It has to be the ring. Oh, Ra!

649
00:40:20.920 --> 00:40:22.920
Oh, my tongue and eyes
are still on the line here.

650
00:40:24.080 --> 00:40:26.480
Look, I may not want
to spend eternity with you

651
00:40:26.560 --> 00:40:28.800
but even an ex-charioteer
doesn't deserve that.

652
00:40:29.560 --> 00:40:31.960
Thank you, Princess.
That's very kind of you.

653
00:40:32.040 --> 00:40:34.120
But we have to start again,
and time is running out.

654
00:40:34.320 --> 00:40:35.560
Well, we can't do anything now.

655
00:40:35.640 --> 00:40:37.496
Let's rest, and we'll find the ring
in the morning.

656
00:40:37.520 --> 00:40:39.520
Ed's a nice guy.
He offered to take us home.

657
00:40:39.600 --> 00:40:40.600
Ed?

658
00:40:40.680 --> 00:40:43.160
A guy that puts 90 horses
under a chariot box is nice?

659
00:40:43.240 --> 00:40:44.240
I'd rather sleep here.

660
00:40:46.600 --> 00:40:48.200
Hair? Wet? No way.

661
00:40:55.120 --> 00:40:56.600
- Hey!
- Hi, Ed.

662
00:40:57.040 --> 00:40:58.720
We need a place to spend the night.

663
00:41:00.120 --> 00:41:02.040
Sure! Yeah. Come on in.

664
00:41:02.360 --> 00:41:03.360
Thank you.

665
00:41:03.720 --> 00:41:05.120
Oh, nice dog.

666
00:41:07.640 --> 00:41:08.800
Thanks, Ed.

667
00:41:12.080 --> 00:41:13.080
Hey, hey!

668
00:41:21.880 --> 00:41:25.160
So, would you sing the song for me?

669
00:41:26.000 --> 00:41:27.720
- Yes.
- Yes!

670
00:41:27.840 --> 00:41:30.040
You won't be sorry.
It's gonna be a hit!

671
00:41:30.960 --> 00:41:33.280
Hear that? It's gonna be a hit.

672
00:41:34.600 --> 00:41:35.600
Ed, what's a "hit"?

673
00:41:38.480 --> 00:41:40.880
Yes! Funny and beautiful.

674
00:41:40.960 --> 00:41:41.960
Let's go to the studio.

675
00:41:45.840 --> 00:41:47.480
I feel cool, dude.

676
00:41:48.520 --> 00:41:49.560
You look great, bro.

677
00:42:14.880 --> 00:42:15.880
Yeah.

678
00:42:15.960 --> 00:42:18.040
Can you imagine putting up with that
your whole life?

679
00:42:19.000 --> 00:42:21.560
Don't get me wrong.
She has some positive qualities.

680
00:42:21.920 --> 00:42:25.080
She's determined,
strong, intelligent.

681
00:42:25.800 --> 00:42:26.960
Maybe it wouldn't be so bad.

682
00:42:28.600 --> 00:42:29.680
But you know...

683
00:42:30.160 --> 00:42:31.160
She snores.

684
00:42:31.680 --> 00:42:32.680
Like a walrus.

685
00:42:38.560 --> 00:42:39.560
What's going on?

686
00:42:39.800 --> 00:42:41.600
The singer that ruined the play.

687
00:42:41.960 --> 00:42:43.600
She was wearing a symbol.

688
00:42:44.000 --> 00:42:46.080
The same symbol that is in the ring.

689
00:42:46.160 --> 00:42:48.240
- So?
- So the legend behind the ring

690
00:42:48.480 --> 00:42:49.480
is true.

691
00:42:53.880 --> 00:42:55.760
She has come back to get her ring.

692
00:42:55.840 --> 00:42:57.360
And I have it.

693
00:43:01.400 --> 00:43:03.720
What could be
a more amazing discovery

694
00:43:03.800 --> 00:43:07.000
than an undiscovered
royal Egyptian ring?

695
00:43:08.440 --> 00:43:10.160
Two undiscovered
royal Egyptian rings!

696
00:43:10.240 --> 00:43:11.640
Two? There are two?

697
00:43:11.720 --> 00:43:13.520
- Amazing.
- No, you morons!

698
00:43:13.600 --> 00:43:15.560
I'm talking about a living mummy!

699
00:43:15.640 --> 00:43:16.880
<i>Calling Mommy.</i>

700
00:43:18.680 --> 00:43:19.880
<i>Calling Mommy.</i>

701
00:43:21.080 --> 00:43:22.400
<i>Sylvester!</i>

702
00:43:22.480 --> 00:43:23.880
Mommy? I can't talk now.

703
00:43:23.960 --> 00:43:26.280
<i>What? Don't you want to talk
to your mother?</i>

704
00:43:26.360 --> 00:43:27.360
Oh, no...

705
00:43:27.440 --> 00:43:28.440
No, Mommy, it's not that.

706
00:43:28.960 --> 00:43:30.840
We don't need the phone because...

707
00:43:31.200 --> 00:43:32.520
I'm right beside you!

708
00:43:34.360 --> 00:43:35.360
Listen to me, Mother.

709
00:43:35.520 --> 00:43:36.720
There's an echo.

710
00:43:37.560 --> 00:43:38.840
I have made the most important

711
00:43:38.920 --> 00:43:40.760
archaeological discovery of all time.

712
00:43:41.320 --> 00:43:42.320
I guarantee you

713
00:43:42.520 --> 00:43:45.240
the whole world
will now know the name

714
00:43:45.440 --> 00:43:47.320
of Lord Sylvester Carnaby.

715
00:43:53.120 --> 00:43:54.120
Why?

716
00:43:54.200 --> 00:43:56.000
<i>No matter what time
No matter the place!</i>

717
00:43:56.080 --> 00:43:59.360
<i>Rise and shine it's a beautiful day!</i>

718
00:43:59.560 --> 00:44:00.560
Morning, my star.

719
00:44:00.640 --> 00:44:02.960
Morning, little bro, dog,
and you too.

720
00:44:03.040 --> 00:44:04.520
Listen, big day ahead of us.

721
00:44:04.600 --> 00:44:06.920
I want to stream a video

722
00:44:07.000 --> 00:44:09.320
of Nefer's performance.

723
00:44:09.880 --> 00:44:12.480
Thoughts. Feelings and thoughts.
What say you guys?

724
00:44:12.640 --> 00:44:14.240
Oh, yeah, great.

725
00:44:14.640 --> 00:44:16.240
But we have things to do.

726
00:44:16.320 --> 00:44:17.480
- Oh, come on.
- Cool.

727
00:44:17.560 --> 00:44:19.760
But are these the only garbs you got
from the musical?

728
00:44:20.640 --> 00:44:21.640
Well, we...

729
00:44:22.640 --> 00:44:23.640
lost our baggage.

730
00:44:23.920 --> 00:44:26.040
Jeez, that happens to me
all the time when I fly.

731
00:44:26.240 --> 00:44:28.400
- You fly?
- Here. Take my card.

732
00:44:28.560 --> 00:44:29.776
There's a shop across the road.

733
00:44:29.800 --> 00:44:31.400
'Cause vintage is out

734
00:44:31.480 --> 00:44:33.560
and my star needs a new look.

735
00:44:36.000 --> 00:44:37.720
Don't worry. That means he likes you.

736
00:44:38.160 --> 00:44:40.080
I don't know what's worse.
Freaky dog.

737
00:44:40.160 --> 00:44:41.480
You need to feed that thing.

738
00:44:45.000 --> 00:44:46.000
Look!

739
00:44:48.960 --> 00:44:51.040
Okay. Follow me!

740
00:44:51.120 --> 00:44:52.600
- Thut!
- Thut!

741
00:44:52.680 --> 00:44:54.320
Look out, Thut! Over there!

742
00:44:54.400 --> 00:44:55.800
- Look out!
- Thut!

743
00:45:07.280 --> 00:45:09.360
There! I don't think
anybody noticed us, do you?

744
00:45:11.120 --> 00:45:13.320
At least there won't be
any wedding night surprises.

745
00:45:17.000 --> 00:45:18.160
A little help here, please.

746
00:45:19.280 --> 00:45:20.280
There!

747
00:45:23.280 --> 00:45:24.280
Thanks!

748
00:45:25.040 --> 00:45:26.520
No time to waste. Let's go.

749
00:46:17.120 --> 00:46:18.120
<i>Attention.</i>

750
00:46:18.400 --> 00:46:20.960
- <i>We kindly remind customers...</i>
- Where did that voice come from?

751
00:46:21.040 --> 00:46:23.200
<i>That this store will be closing
in five minutes.</i>

752
00:46:23.560 --> 00:46:24.560
From the sky!

753
00:46:25.480 --> 00:46:27.960
It's Ra! The voice of the Sun God.

754
00:46:29.000 --> 00:46:31.400
Oh, Ra, God of the Sun

755
00:46:31.480 --> 00:46:34.000
God of Life, light our path!

756
00:46:34.320 --> 00:46:36.200
What should we do, oh, Ra?

757
00:46:36.400 --> 00:46:38.560
<i>Please, kindly finish your shopping.</i>

758
00:46:38.640 --> 00:46:41.600
- We have.
- <i>And proceed towards the exits.</i>

759
00:46:41.680 --> 00:46:44.040
As you command, oh, great Ra.

760
00:46:44.640 --> 00:46:45.640
That way!

761
00:46:46.080 --> 00:46:48.480
Thank you, magnificent Ra!

762
00:46:54.680 --> 00:46:56.320
Yeah! Lookin'...

763
00:46:58.640 --> 00:46:59.640
Yeah!

764
00:47:01.320 --> 00:47:02.840
Listen, I've got the song loaded up.

765
00:47:02.920 --> 00:47:04.560
We're ready to stream
a live performance!

766
00:47:04.640 --> 00:47:06.800
I've been promoting
through my Insta all afternoon.

767
00:47:06.880 --> 00:47:08.520
Ed, we don't speak Latin.

768
00:47:08.680 --> 00:47:09.880
They won't just hear you...

769
00:47:10.000 --> 00:47:11.560
they're gonna see you as well.

770
00:47:11.640 --> 00:47:13.840
- They'll see me?
- Of course, on the computer.

771
00:47:13.920 --> 00:47:14.920
Will I fit in there?

772
00:47:15.800 --> 00:47:17.400
I love your sense of humor!

773
00:47:17.480 --> 00:47:19.560
No, not you! It is a "streaming."

774
00:47:19.760 --> 00:47:20.760
"Live Internet?"

775
00:47:21.280 --> 00:47:22.480
You don't get it, dude.

776
00:47:24.760 --> 00:47:26.920
You are going to slay.

777
00:47:27.000 --> 00:47:28.000
Slay?

778
00:47:28.080 --> 00:47:29.960
It means, "do a good job," right bro?

779
00:47:30.800 --> 00:47:32.160
I don't think this is a good idea.

780
00:47:32.920 --> 00:47:34.160
It's the first time

781
00:47:34.240 --> 00:47:36.320
someone has ever asked me to sing.

782
00:47:36.400 --> 00:47:37.400
- But Nefer...
- Thut!

783
00:47:37.480 --> 00:47:38.840
Time is running out.

784
00:47:40.960 --> 00:47:42.920
I have fought all my life

785
00:47:43.200 --> 00:47:44.600
to make my own decisions.

786
00:47:50.800 --> 00:47:51.800
Then make this decision.

787
00:47:52.360 --> 00:47:53.360
I'll support you.

788
00:47:55.760 --> 00:47:56.760
Thanks, Thut.

789
00:47:56.840 --> 00:47:58.240
That means a lot.

790
00:48:00.280 --> 00:48:01.680
Well, do your thing.

791
00:48:03.040 --> 00:48:04.840
Yeah, I guess I'll just...

792
00:48:05.360 --> 00:48:07.000
- do it.
- Gimme five!

793
00:48:07.080 --> 00:48:08.080
Up top!

794
00:48:11.680 --> 00:48:12.680
Yeah!

795
00:48:12.760 --> 00:48:13.760
Yeah!

796
00:48:20.640 --> 00:48:23.280
<i>I'm afraid I'm slipping away</i>

797
00:48:23.800 --> 00:48:27.520
<i>I'm going to waste
I'm never gonna change</i>

798
00:48:27.920 --> 00:48:31.160
<i>Don't wanna leave the world
The way that's it's now</i>

799
00:48:31.320 --> 00:48:34.560
<i>I don't wanna miss
Any good chance to feel proud</i>

800
00:48:34.640 --> 00:48:36.280
<i>Just raise your hands now</i>

801
00:48:36.560 --> 00:48:37.880
<i>Just raise your hands and sing</i>

802
00:48:37.960 --> 00:48:40.520
<i>Bah-bah, bah-bah, bah-bah</i>

803
00:48:40.680 --> 00:48:41.720
<i>Bah-bah-bah</i>

804
00:48:42.080 --> 00:48:44.920
<i>But you can't seize me</i>

805
00:48:45.520 --> 00:48:48.640
<i>You can redeem me</i>

806
00:48:49.160 --> 00:48:51.880
<i>You've got the keys to free me</i>

807
00:48:51.960 --> 00:48:54.560
<i>So don't delay</i>

808
00:48:54.960 --> 00:48:58.200
<i>I'm today yesterday's tomorrow</i>

809
00:48:58.440 --> 00:49:01.600
<i>I'm today the time you borrowed</i>

810
00:49:02.000 --> 00:49:04.800
<i>I'm today the stars align</i>

811
00:49:04.880 --> 00:49:08.440
<i>Don't pass me by</i>

812
00:49:08.760 --> 00:49:10.200
<i>'Cause I'm today</i>

813
00:49:10.280 --> 00:49:12.120
<i>Yesterday's tomorrow</i>

814
00:49:12.640 --> 00:49:15.720
<i>I'm today the time you borrowed</i>

815
00:49:16.120 --> 00:49:18.880
<i>I'm today the stars align</i>

816
00:49:19.080 --> 00:49:22.560
<i>Don't pass me by</i>

817
00:49:22.640 --> 00:49:24.440
<i>This mystery girl
has managed to score</i>

818
00:49:24.520 --> 00:49:26.680
<i>over 10 million hits
across the globe.</i>

819
00:49:27.040 --> 00:49:29.120
<i>The girl that shocked audiences
on the West End</i>

820
00:49:29.200 --> 00:49:30.880
<i>has now revealed herself to the world</i>

821
00:49:30.960 --> 00:49:32.360
<i>and she's not stopping there.</i>

822
00:49:32.880 --> 00:49:34.840
<i>Reporting live
from the Commons at Knightsbridge</i>

823
00:49:35.040 --> 00:49:36.160
<i>I'm George Towers.</i>

824
00:49:37.200 --> 00:49:38.680
We've got her!

825
00:49:54.480 --> 00:49:55.480
You know what?

826
00:49:55.560 --> 00:49:57.200
Perhaps this is my place.

827
00:49:57.920 --> 00:49:59.160
I've only been here a few days

828
00:49:59.240 --> 00:50:01.240
and already my dreams
are coming true.

829
00:50:03.240 --> 00:50:04.560
That's really good...

830
00:50:05.400 --> 00:50:06.400
for you.

831
00:50:07.880 --> 00:50:09.080
Oh, come on, you'll be fine.

832
00:50:09.440 --> 00:50:10.440
I gave you my word

833
00:50:10.520 --> 00:50:12.200
I would help you find the ring,
and I will.

834
00:50:12.360 --> 00:50:13.360
We'll find it.

835
00:50:25.760 --> 00:50:27.160
He's not like the rest.

836
00:50:27.920 --> 00:50:28.920
Maybe we...

837
00:50:29.080 --> 00:50:30.800
Come on, what am I saying?

838
00:50:32.080 --> 00:50:33.200
I know. I know.

839
00:50:33.280 --> 00:50:34.800
We're from two different worlds
anyway.

840
00:50:42.360 --> 00:50:43.840
Croc! It's Croc!

841
00:50:44.000 --> 00:50:45.080
Something's wrong with him!

842
00:50:48.680 --> 00:50:49.680
Nefer!

843
00:50:51.760 --> 00:50:52.760
Nefer! No!

844
00:51:09.920 --> 00:51:10.920
Nefer!

845
00:51:11.800 --> 00:51:12.960
Where are they taking her?

846
00:51:13.040 --> 00:51:14.240
I recognize those men.

847
00:51:14.320 --> 00:51:15.776
They're the ones
who took the ring from the ship.

848
00:51:15.800 --> 00:51:17.120
We need to follow that chariot.

849
00:51:17.400 --> 00:51:18.960
It belongs to the Carnaby Museum.

850
00:51:19.200 --> 00:51:20.736
How did you know that?
Are you in on this?

851
00:51:20.760 --> 00:51:21.920
Was this your plan all along?

852
00:51:22.000 --> 00:51:23.120
What? In on this?

853
00:51:23.200 --> 00:51:25.200
The van belongs
to the Carnaby Museum.

854
00:51:25.280 --> 00:51:26.680
It said it on the side!

855
00:51:26.920 --> 00:51:28.520
I blame you for this, Ed.

856
00:51:28.760 --> 00:51:30.400
So stay out of my way, got it?

857
00:51:31.120 --> 00:51:34.080
I'll get to that museum.
I've got a princess to save.

858
00:51:34.160 --> 00:51:35.760
You're crazy. You'll never get in.

859
00:51:36.000 --> 00:51:38.080
Their security is mental!

860
00:51:40.160 --> 00:51:41.800
No. You stay here.

861
00:51:42.160 --> 00:51:43.160
It's dangerous.

862
00:51:43.240 --> 00:51:44.760
I'm your brother,
and you will obey me.

863
00:52:12.480 --> 00:52:13.480
<i>Princess...</i>

864
00:52:21.720 --> 00:52:22.720
<i>Princess...</i>

865
00:52:23.520 --> 00:52:24.720
Princess Nefer.

866
00:52:25.200 --> 00:52:27.080
So delightful to meet you.

867
00:52:27.920 --> 00:52:28.920
Let me...

868
00:52:29.520 --> 00:52:30.520
Let me go.

869
00:52:30.760 --> 00:52:33.320
Unfortunately, I can't do that.

870
00:52:33.720 --> 00:52:36.560
This morning is the opening
of my greatest exhibition yet.

871
00:52:41.880 --> 00:52:43.200
Originally, the centerpiece

872
00:52:43.280 --> 00:52:44.880
was going to be your ring.

873
00:52:45.920 --> 00:52:46.920
But now...

874
00:52:47.120 --> 00:52:48.120
you.

875
00:52:48.280 --> 00:52:50.760
You are my greatest discovery.

876
00:52:51.480 --> 00:52:55.480
And when I reveal you to the world,
yours won't be the only name

877
00:52:55.560 --> 00:52:56.960
that goes down in history.

878
00:52:57.920 --> 00:53:01.000
And if you thought your little song
made you famous...

879
00:53:01.560 --> 00:53:04.280
wait until they find out
what you really are!

880
00:53:04.800 --> 00:53:06.440
You can't do this.

881
00:53:07.160 --> 00:53:09.000
- Thut... Thut will...
- I can see you!

882
00:53:09.640 --> 00:53:10.760
He will come for me.

883
00:53:13.320 --> 00:53:14.320
There you are!

884
00:53:14.400 --> 00:53:16.880
That's what will sell
the most tickets.

885
00:53:17.880 --> 00:53:18.880
Now...

886
00:53:19.160 --> 00:53:22.080
if you'll excuse me,
I've an exhibition to prepare.

887
00:53:56.000 --> 00:53:57.920
Wait, this is all my stuff!

888
00:53:59.120 --> 00:54:01.000
An entire section dedicated to me.

889
00:54:01.320 --> 00:54:03.200
"The treasures of Thut
the Fleet of Foot."

890
00:54:03.680 --> 00:54:04.680
What a nickname!

891
00:54:05.160 --> 00:54:07.080
One hundred-time
chariot racing champion?

892
00:54:07.160 --> 00:54:09.120
What? It's 112 plus one.

893
00:54:09.880 --> 00:54:10.880
Idiots.

894
00:54:13.200 --> 00:54:14.200
Nefer?

895
00:54:15.760 --> 00:54:16.760
Nefer!

896
00:54:17.720 --> 00:54:19.600
Oh, no. What have they done to you?

897
00:54:19.760 --> 00:54:22.400
You look like humans,
but you're really

898
00:54:22.480 --> 00:54:24.360
ancient Egyptian mummies.

899
00:54:25.680 --> 00:54:27.400
- You!
- Welcome

900
00:54:27.480 --> 00:54:29.360
to your new home.

901
00:54:30.400 --> 00:54:31.400
Not so fast!

902
00:55:15.400 --> 00:55:17.200
Look, bro. I can help.

903
00:55:17.680 --> 00:55:18.880
Let's rescue the grumpy guy.

904
00:55:20.040 --> 00:55:21.040
Really?

905
00:55:24.400 --> 00:55:25.400
I can't.

906
00:55:25.880 --> 00:55:27.760
Oh, jeez. I'm in bad shape.

907
00:55:27.840 --> 00:55:29.640
Don't worry. You stay here, watching.

908
00:55:30.880 --> 00:55:32.800
Hold it. I see a hawk.

909
00:55:46.720 --> 00:55:48.080
You sure this is okay, Danny?

910
00:55:48.520 --> 00:55:51.080
Lord Carnaby said
not to leave the princess unattended.

911
00:55:51.840 --> 00:55:53.216
We're the only ones in the building.

912
00:55:53.240 --> 00:55:55.400
Besides,
how can we protect the princess

913
00:55:55.480 --> 00:55:56.480
on an empty stomach?

914
00:55:57.560 --> 00:55:58.800
All right. Makes sense.

915
00:56:09.200 --> 00:56:10.200
What have we done?

916
00:56:15.960 --> 00:56:16.960
Perfect.

917
00:56:32.240 --> 00:56:33.240
Thut?

918
00:56:35.280 --> 00:56:37.680
You know what? I think you're cute.

919
00:56:38.600 --> 00:56:40.320
Thanks. You're pretty.

920
00:56:40.400 --> 00:56:41.720
We've got to get them out, quick!

921
00:56:41.960 --> 00:56:43.880
I told you to keep watch
over the princess.

922
00:56:43.960 --> 00:56:45.120
Sorry, Mr. Carnaby.

923
00:56:45.520 --> 00:56:47.520
You see, we wanted some snacks and...

924
00:56:47.600 --> 00:56:50.480
Then we got stuck
in the vending machine.

925
00:56:58.280 --> 00:56:59.280
What was that?

926
00:57:00.280 --> 00:57:01.560
It's coming from the exhibition.

927
00:57:01.600 --> 00:57:02.600
It's the princess!

928
00:57:03.440 --> 00:57:05.600
Well, don't just stand there,
you blithering idiots!

929
00:57:06.160 --> 00:57:07.680
My... my chocky bar's...

930
00:57:07.960 --> 00:57:09.280
Get the princess!

931
00:57:11.320 --> 00:57:12.320
Are you okay?

932
00:57:12.400 --> 00:57:13.400
Hey, Thut...

933
00:57:13.480 --> 00:57:15.560
Sekhem is so...

934
00:57:16.400 --> 00:57:18.560
- so hero-ish.
- Thanks.

935
00:57:18.640 --> 00:57:20.320
He learned it all from me.

936
00:57:20.840 --> 00:57:21.840
Okay, come on.

937
00:57:24.800 --> 00:57:25.800
Someone's been here.

938
00:57:26.280 --> 00:57:27.680
Keep your eyes peeled.

939
00:57:29.520 --> 00:57:31.080
It's them! Quick, hide!

940
00:57:35.400 --> 00:57:36.760
I... I am a woman

941
00:57:36.840 --> 00:57:40.120
and I can stand on my own two feet.

942
00:57:41.800 --> 00:57:42.880
What was that?

943
00:57:46.440 --> 00:57:49.400
- Did I tell you that you're cute?
- Yeah, I...

944
00:57:49.560 --> 00:57:50.960
I feel very strongly that you...

945
00:57:52.680 --> 00:57:53.680
They're kissing!

946
00:58:01.320 --> 00:58:02.320
The ring!

947
00:58:03.400 --> 00:58:04.400
No.

948
00:58:04.600 --> 00:58:05.600
She's escaped!

949
00:58:05.680 --> 00:58:07.720
You fools! You imbeciles!

950
00:58:07.920 --> 00:58:09.160
I give you one job...

951
00:58:10.520 --> 00:58:12.560
I got it! Let's get out of here.

952
00:58:13.200 --> 00:58:14.200
Guys?

953
00:58:16.360 --> 00:58:18.320
We escaped your little trap!

954
00:58:18.520 --> 00:58:20.120
Now, we'll ruin

955
00:58:20.200 --> 00:58:22.480
your special little opening day.

956
00:58:23.480 --> 00:58:24.480
Stop!

957
00:58:32.200 --> 00:58:34.000
Sorry about that!
Can't take them anywhere.

958
00:58:34.480 --> 00:58:35.480
Go!

959
00:58:35.720 --> 00:58:36.720
Get them.

960
00:58:47.760 --> 00:58:48.760
Hey!

961
00:58:59.080 --> 00:59:00.080
Come on!

962
00:59:07.840 --> 00:59:09.440
Hey, look! Let's get that!

963
00:59:12.520 --> 00:59:13.640
There they go! Quick!

964
00:59:14.280 --> 00:59:16.680
- Chariot driver, drive the chariot!
- Well, I've...

965
00:59:17.040 --> 00:59:18.680
never driven a chariot like this.

966
00:59:18.760 --> 00:59:20.480
I did! I can do it!

967
00:59:20.880 --> 00:59:22.960
- Please!
- What, seriously, the kid?

968
00:59:24.760 --> 00:59:25.760
Go!

969
00:59:25.840 --> 00:59:27.320
Croc, buddy, get the pedals.

970
00:59:34.200 --> 00:59:35.920
Get the van. Get the van!

971
00:59:41.040 --> 00:59:43.800
- Where do I go?
- <i>This is the bus to the South Bank.</i>

972
00:59:43.880 --> 00:59:45.360
Yeah! Ra is with us!

973
00:59:45.640 --> 00:59:47.360
- Ra is a woman?
- Got a problem with that?

974
00:59:48.720 --> 00:59:50.600
Why are you going so slowly?

975
00:59:50.680 --> 00:59:52.160
I'm obeying the rules of the road.

976
00:59:52.240 --> 00:59:54.160
- The speed limit is...
- Forget the speed limit.

977
00:59:54.240 --> 00:59:55.560
Get out of the way. Let me.

978
00:59:56.440 --> 00:59:57.440
Right. Here we go.

979
01:00:01.040 --> 01:00:02.040
Croc, come on!

980
01:00:07.040 --> 01:00:08.760
Slow down...

981
01:00:08.840 --> 01:00:10.240
You don't slow down in a chase!

982
01:00:10.480 --> 01:00:12.400
Not slowing down is the whole point!

983
01:00:12.960 --> 01:00:14.000
I can't watch!

984
01:00:14.560 --> 01:00:16.800
<i>Next stop, Russell Square Station.</i>

985
01:00:16.880 --> 01:00:18.960
<i>Final destination, South Bank.</i>

986
01:00:19.240 --> 01:00:21.560
Ra says to stop next!
Do what Ra says!

987
01:00:21.640 --> 01:00:23.280
No, he says to stop at the pier!

988
01:00:23.360 --> 01:00:24.360
Don't worry, big brother.

989
01:00:24.520 --> 01:00:26.240
- He who dares wins!
- Dies!

990
01:00:26.320 --> 01:00:28.960
We're gonna die!

991
01:00:29.080 --> 01:00:32.000
They won't get away from me.
I want my mummy!

992
01:00:32.080 --> 01:00:34.160
- <i>Calling Mommy.</i>
- I meant that mummy!

993
01:00:34.240 --> 01:00:35.480
- <i>Calling Mommy.</i>
- No, I know...

994
01:00:35.800 --> 01:00:37.360
<i>Sylvester? What are you doing?</i>

995
01:00:37.440 --> 01:00:39.160
Not now, mother! I'm driving!

996
01:00:39.240 --> 01:00:41.120
<i>It's not safe to drive
and talk on the phone.</i>

997
01:00:47.360 --> 01:00:48.360
Croc!

998
01:01:05.520 --> 01:01:06.520
I'll show you!

999
01:01:07.600 --> 01:01:08.600
I can't shake him.

1000
01:01:09.080 --> 01:01:10.080
What do I do?

1001
01:01:10.960 --> 01:01:11.960
Thut!

1002
01:01:18.640 --> 01:01:19.720
See that ramp up ahead?

1003
01:01:20.000 --> 01:01:21.120
Drive right for it.

1004
01:01:21.200 --> 01:01:22.760
But that boat, it's already leaving.

1005
01:01:22.840 --> 01:01:24.440
Then we'd better go faster.

1006
01:01:37.880 --> 01:01:39.520
Now! Turn and slam the brakes!

1007
01:01:58.120 --> 01:02:00.240
You made it! Way to go boss!

1008
01:02:00.400 --> 01:02:02.600
Yeah, but the people we were chasing
are back there.

1009
01:02:02.920 --> 01:02:04.856
- Guess we can't get 'em now.
- Shut up, would you?

1010
01:02:04.880 --> 01:02:07.080
I will chase them
to the end of the world

1011
01:02:07.160 --> 01:02:08.160
if necessary.

1012
01:02:09.200 --> 01:02:11.400
You haven't seen the last of me!

1013
01:02:11.760 --> 01:02:12.760
Bye.

1014
01:02:13.360 --> 01:02:14.360
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

1015
01:02:15.200 --> 01:02:16.440
- We're safe!
- Well done!

1016
01:02:23.040 --> 01:02:24.040
You were great, Sekhem.

1017
01:02:24.880 --> 01:02:25.880
Thanks, big bro.

1018
01:02:27.000 --> 01:02:28.000
Are you okay?

1019
01:02:28.160 --> 01:02:29.640
Yes. Thank you.

1020
01:02:32.560 --> 01:02:34.040
So, fancy explaining

1021
01:02:34.120 --> 01:02:36.360
why a chariot racer
is frightened of going fast?

1022
01:02:36.600 --> 01:02:38.200
Oh, that. Oh, well...

1023
01:02:38.400 --> 01:02:41.200
It's just that
I don't feel comfortable

1024
01:02:41.280 --> 01:02:42.720
driving a chariot with no horses.

1025
01:02:42.800 --> 01:02:44.040
I don't trust what I can't see.

1026
01:02:46.440 --> 01:02:48.320
Yeah, look, I'm sorry about,
you know...

1027
01:02:49.000 --> 01:02:50.056
kissing you at the museum, I just...

1028
01:02:50.080 --> 01:02:51.880
- Oh, yeah. I...
- I just wasn't think...

1029
01:02:51.960 --> 01:02:53.576
- No, I'm sorry for that.
- And this dart that, yeah...

1030
01:02:53.600 --> 01:02:55.680
I mean, I'm also sorry
about the kissing.

1031
01:02:55.760 --> 01:02:57.320
Yeah, well, good...

1032
01:02:57.400 --> 01:02:58.880
that we can be honest
with each other.

1033
01:02:59.280 --> 01:03:00.280
Great chat.

1034
01:03:00.360 --> 01:03:02.160
Okay, mummies,
back to the After World.

1035
01:03:02.240 --> 01:03:03.800
Let's walk like Egyptians!

1036
01:03:04.520 --> 01:03:06.600
Yeah. We've only got two suns
before the curse falls

1037
01:03:06.680 --> 01:03:07.880
and I lose my eyes and tongue.

1038
01:03:08.200 --> 01:03:09.320
I mean, you know, the usual.

1039
01:03:09.960 --> 01:03:11.256
Well, let's just use the stargate.

1040
01:03:11.280 --> 01:03:12.280
It's over there.

1041
01:03:12.440 --> 01:03:13.440
That's...

1042
01:03:13.520 --> 01:03:15.960
That's not a stargate.
That's a Ferris wheel.

1043
01:03:16.280 --> 01:03:18.280
Oh, so no time travel?

1044
01:03:18.360 --> 01:03:21.080
Just all the time at the same place.

1045
01:03:21.560 --> 01:03:23.880
Oh, Ra. Unless flying like a falcon

1046
01:03:23.960 --> 01:03:26.000
is a thing in the human world,
we're finished.

1047
01:03:27.280 --> 01:03:28.840
Actually, it is.

1048
01:03:30.200 --> 01:03:31.200
Yeah, wow!

1049
01:03:32.480 --> 01:03:33.600
- She's gorgeous.
- Let me...

1050
01:03:33.880 --> 01:03:35.560
- Is that relevant?
- No. Wait.

1051
01:03:35.840 --> 01:03:37.160
Wait for it...

1052
01:03:38.200 --> 01:03:39.200
Yes!

1053
01:03:40.320 --> 01:03:42.640
Wait, no...

1054
01:03:44.360 --> 01:03:45.360
That one right there!

1055
01:03:46.520 --> 01:03:47.920
The God Horus?

1056
01:03:48.120 --> 01:03:49.800
Horus himself is gonna take us?

1057
01:03:50.880 --> 01:03:52.280
You could be in Egypt

1058
01:03:52.360 --> 01:03:53.680
in five minutes...

1059
01:03:53.760 --> 01:03:55.080
Hours! Five hours!

1060
01:03:55.160 --> 01:03:56.160
- Perfect.
- Yes!

1061
01:04:03.920 --> 01:04:05.360
Well, I think...

1062
01:04:05.760 --> 01:04:07.680
it's time for you to choose,
Princess.

1063
01:05:20.320 --> 01:05:21.320
So...

1064
01:05:22.440 --> 01:05:24.000
Can you imagine if we'd had to marry?

1065
01:05:24.080 --> 01:05:25.080
You and me?

1066
01:05:25.440 --> 01:05:26.560
We'd be like oil and water.

1067
01:05:26.760 --> 01:05:27.760
Totally.

1068
01:05:34.560 --> 01:05:35.560
But you know, I...

1069
01:05:35.960 --> 01:05:37.160
should probably thank you.

1070
01:05:38.160 --> 01:05:40.040
You were very brave, charioteer.

1071
01:05:41.480 --> 01:05:43.360
No. Not at all.

1072
01:05:44.160 --> 01:05:46.760
In fact, I'm not actually
who you think I am.

1073
01:05:48.640 --> 01:05:50.720
I retired because I got scared.

1074
01:05:54.200 --> 01:05:56.600
And since then, speed makes me panic.

1075
01:05:58.120 --> 01:05:59.280
So, no.

1076
01:06:00.320 --> 01:06:02.400
I'm not brave. Not at all.

1077
01:06:09.960 --> 01:06:11.320
If you weren't brave...

1078
01:06:11.960 --> 01:06:14.120
you wouldn't have risked your life
to rescue me.

1079
01:06:19.840 --> 01:06:21.400
You're braver than you think, Thut.

1080
01:06:23.920 --> 01:06:24.920
Yeah, well...

1081
01:06:25.400 --> 01:06:26.400
I don't know.

1082
01:06:32.720 --> 01:06:34.120
- Get off! That's mine!
- No!

1083
01:06:37.760 --> 01:06:38.760
Give it here! Give it!

1084
01:06:43.600 --> 01:06:45.016
Look, just 'cause you went
to the posh school...

1085
01:06:45.040 --> 01:06:46.240
Oh, yeah...

1086
01:06:46.320 --> 01:06:47.440
I know who's Mum's favorite.

1087
01:07:49.400 --> 01:07:50.400
- So...
- You...

1088
01:07:51.160 --> 01:07:52.720
Sorry... Like, you know...

1089
01:07:53.560 --> 01:07:55.800
Well, I suppose...

1090
01:07:56.600 --> 01:07:58.560
it's goodbye, Princess.

1091
01:07:59.480 --> 01:08:00.960
Goodbye, charioteer.

1092
01:08:17.960 --> 01:08:18.960
Turn around.

1093
01:08:29.520 --> 01:08:31.120
Turn around, please.

1094
01:09:07.640 --> 01:09:10.560
I'm sorry, Father.
I was afraid that...

1095
01:09:10.640 --> 01:09:12.600
You can't imagine
how worried I have been.

1096
01:10:30.240 --> 01:10:32.480
A city of living mummies.

1097
01:10:33.560 --> 01:10:35.520
The legend lives.

1098
01:10:36.360 --> 01:10:37.800
It wasn't a legend after all.

1099
01:10:38.000 --> 01:10:40.400
Not after today, Danny.
Not after today.

1100
01:10:40.480 --> 01:10:42.800
He's Danny, I'm Dennis.

1101
01:10:42.880 --> 01:10:44.480
Do not ruin the moment.

1102
01:10:45.800 --> 01:10:47.040
Where is the princess?

1103
01:10:47.480 --> 01:10:48.480
Princess?

1104
01:10:49.040 --> 01:10:51.760
Who needs a princess
when you can have a pharaoh?

1105
01:10:54.960 --> 01:10:57.280
Sire, they've managed
to infiltrate the city

1106
01:10:57.360 --> 01:10:58.560
using the metal beasts.

1107
01:11:00.200 --> 01:11:01.520
Take everybody to the shelter.

1108
01:11:02.000 --> 01:11:03.760
I'll deploy the city's defenses.

1109
01:11:03.960 --> 01:11:04.960
Go with them.

1110
01:11:18.200 --> 01:11:20.640
Lord Carnaby requests an audience

1111
01:11:20.720 --> 01:11:21.800
with the Pharaoh.

1112
01:11:26.400 --> 01:11:28.000
They took away my exhibition.

1113
01:11:28.360 --> 01:11:29.960
They scoff at my name.

1114
01:11:30.440 --> 01:11:31.760
But I will show them

1115
01:11:31.840 --> 01:11:33.720
a living pharaoh.

1116
01:11:34.160 --> 01:11:36.040
Then they'll see.

1117
01:11:39.880 --> 01:11:41.080
Nefer, stay back!

1118
01:11:41.160 --> 01:11:42.240
This is my fault.

1119
01:11:42.800 --> 01:11:44.040
He followed me here.

1120
01:11:44.720 --> 01:11:45.920
This is my fight too.

1121
01:11:57.600 --> 01:11:59.520
Thut. Thut!

1122
01:12:00.240 --> 01:12:01.240
He's here!

1123
01:12:03.160 --> 01:12:04.720
The one from the museum, he's come!

1124
01:12:04.960 --> 01:12:05.960
We're under attack!

1125
01:12:06.680 --> 01:12:08.040
If he wants to come, let him come.

1126
01:12:08.360 --> 01:12:10.440
It's that or an eternity
signing autographs.

1127
01:12:11.040 --> 01:12:12.560
- Alone.
- Oh, come on!

1128
01:12:12.760 --> 01:12:14.080
The princess needs you!

1129
01:12:14.320 --> 01:12:15.320
She's got guards.

1130
01:12:17.600 --> 01:12:19.600
She needs the bravest among us.

1131
01:12:19.800 --> 01:12:21.520
The supreme champion.

1132
01:12:21.880 --> 01:12:23.120
And that's you.

1133
01:12:23.400 --> 01:12:24.480
"He who dares."

1134
01:12:24.920 --> 01:12:26.320
That's my older brother.

1135
01:12:26.520 --> 01:12:28.320
That's who I look up to and idolize.

1136
01:12:28.560 --> 01:12:31.080
Stop feeling sorry for yourself
and go help her.

1137
01:12:54.880 --> 01:12:55.880
Father!

1138
01:12:56.080 --> 01:12:57.080
No...

1139
01:12:57.560 --> 01:12:58.560
Father!

1140
01:13:19.760 --> 01:13:20.760
I don't believe it!

1141
01:13:26.440 --> 01:13:27.920
You're not going anywhere.

1142
01:13:28.720 --> 01:13:29.720
Foolish child!

1143
01:13:30.480 --> 01:13:31.960
You won't get away with this!

1144
01:13:32.040 --> 01:13:33.280
You want to come too?

1145
01:13:33.440 --> 01:13:35.120
Pesky spoiled brat!

1146
01:14:03.160 --> 01:14:04.560
- No.
- Thut!

1147
01:14:04.760 --> 01:14:05.920
The Charioteer!

1148
01:14:08.040 --> 01:14:09.040
He's getting away!

1149
01:14:13.200 --> 01:14:14.200
Go...

1150
01:14:15.120 --> 01:14:16.120
Croc!

1151
01:14:35.560 --> 01:14:36.560
No!

1152
01:14:48.680 --> 01:14:49.680
Here we go.

1153
01:14:57.280 --> 01:14:58.480
Thut, what are you doing?

1154
01:14:59.520 --> 01:15:00.520
Thut!

1155
01:15:01.640 --> 01:15:02.640
Look out!

1156
01:15:05.280 --> 01:15:07.480
Thut, come on!
You can't let him get away!

1157
01:15:07.560 --> 01:15:09.480
You're not alone. You have a team.

1158
01:15:09.680 --> 01:15:11.880
Thut! Not now, come on!

1159
01:15:11.960 --> 01:15:12.960
Snap out of it!

1160
01:15:14.160 --> 01:15:15.400
Thut! Wake up!

1161
01:15:19.880 --> 01:15:22.040
Thut! Wake up, I need you!

1162
01:15:24.880 --> 01:15:26.520
It's time to take the reins!

1163
01:15:50.320 --> 01:15:52.120
Get off me, boy! I've got you now.

1164
01:15:52.440 --> 01:15:53.440
Thut!

1165
01:15:59.720 --> 01:16:00.720
No!

1166
01:16:01.200 --> 01:16:03.680
Now, you'll be my new trophy.

1167
01:16:03.760 --> 01:16:04.840
- Nefer!
- Thut!

1168
01:16:05.400 --> 01:16:06.880
I'll show you, mummy!

1169
01:16:15.360 --> 01:16:16.880
No...

1170
01:16:18.360 --> 01:16:19.360
I love you.

1171
01:16:25.160 --> 01:16:26.160
Thut!

1172
01:16:34.800 --> 01:16:35.800
No. No.

1173
01:16:35.880 --> 01:16:36.880
Thut!

1174
01:16:37.200 --> 01:16:38.600
Thut? No!

1175
01:16:43.600 --> 01:16:44.600
Thut!

1176
01:16:49.320 --> 01:16:50.320
Nefer!

1177
01:16:51.040 --> 01:16:52.040
Father!

1178
01:16:54.840 --> 01:16:56.200
That's my older brother.

1179
01:17:03.440 --> 01:17:06.400
Young charioteer, you saved my life.

1180
01:17:06.840 --> 01:17:09.440
You did it!
You overcame your fear, Thut!

1181
01:17:09.760 --> 01:17:11.240
No, It was you.

1182
01:17:12.360 --> 01:17:14.080
I've been running from fear
this whole time.

1183
01:17:14.440 --> 01:17:15.840
Whether it was fear to race again

1184
01:17:15.920 --> 01:17:17.720
or fear to love somebody.

1185
01:17:19.400 --> 01:17:22.400
The ceremonial ring
I'm supposed to return.

1186
01:17:23.560 --> 01:17:24.560
But instead...

1187
01:17:26.760 --> 01:17:27.760
Will you marry me?

1188
01:17:29.600 --> 01:17:32.760
Well, the Phoenix chose you, so...

1189
01:17:33.400 --> 01:17:35.640
Technically,
I'm duty-bound to marry you.

1190
01:17:37.920 --> 01:17:38.920
Yes, I will!

1191
01:17:40.840 --> 01:17:42.280
The Phoenix was right.

1192
01:17:42.600 --> 01:17:43.960
You're made for each other.

1193
01:17:58.760 --> 01:18:02.400
By the power vested in me
by the Goddess of Love

1194
01:18:02.760 --> 01:18:06.640
I pronounce you wife and husband.

1195
01:18:34.720 --> 01:18:36.880
<i>All the school kids so sick of books</i>

1196
01:18:36.960 --> 01:18:38.960
<i>They like the punk and the metal band</i>

1197
01:18:39.200 --> 01:18:41.280
<i>- When the buzzer rings
- Oh-way-oh</i>

1198
01:18:41.360 --> 01:18:43.400
<i>They're walking like an Egyptian</i>

1199
01:18:43.600 --> 01:18:45.600
<i>All the kids in the marketplace say</i>

1200
01:18:45.680 --> 01:18:47.640
<i>Way-oh-way-oh</i>

1201
01:18:47.720 --> 01:18:52.360
<i>Ohh-way-oh-way-oh</i>

1202
01:18:52.440 --> 01:18:54.520
<i>Walk like an Egyptian</i>

1203
01:18:55.960 --> 01:18:57.760
It's about time things changed...

1204
01:18:58.400 --> 01:18:59.400
I suppose.
